  "question": {
    "text": "An object is thrown vertically upwards. At its maximum height, which of the following quantity becomes zero ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Momentum",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Potential energy",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Acceleration",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Force",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When a ball is thrown vertically upwards, at the maximum height the velocity is zero.</p><p>As momentum is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></math>, so&nbsp;momentum is also zero&nbsp;at&nbsp;maximum height.</p>"
  }
